{"diagnosis": "Fetch test executes 256-word NOP memory (ADDI x0,x0,0 with opcode 7'b0010011) but traps immediately with `TRAP: cpu trap asserted` and `FAIL 0xdead` at CYCLES=2009. `is_alu_reg_imm` at picorv32.v:877 checks `7'b0011011` (RV64 OP-IMM-32) instead of `7'b0010011` (RV32 OP-IMM), so ADDI/NOP never decodes and is treated as illegal. Single-bit opcode typo explains trap on first fetch and no progress; CONE_SLICE fallback-window picosoc/picosoc.v:134-157 only shows CPU instantiation and disagrees with no picorv32 decode, so trace wins.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -874,5 +874,5 @@
 			is_beq_bne_blt_bge_bltu_bgeu <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b1100011;
 			is_lb_lh_lw_lbu_lhu          <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0000011;
 			is_sb_sh_sw                  <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0100011;
-			is_alu_reg_imm               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0011011;
+			is_alu_reg_imm               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0010011;
 			is_alu_reg_reg               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0110011;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP: cpu trap asserted, fetch progress through NOPs"}

